    <section class="hero" id="overview"><div class="hero-content"><span class="eyebrow">CLD-UF-101 · Foundational · Level 1 · Online Self-Paced</span><h1>Claude User Fundamentals</h1><p class="lead">A complete self-paced course for business users who want to use Claude for writing, summarisation, brainstorming, analysis, document workflows, Projects, Memory, and responsible AI use. No coding, jargon, or prior AI experience is required.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a href="#enrol" class="button primary">Enrol / Register</a><a href="#curriculum" class="button secondary">View curriculum</a><a href="#modules" class="button secondary" data-gated-nav>Open learning modules</a></div><div id="accessStatus" class="gate-panel"><span class="access-pill">Locked</span><p><strong>Course content is locked.</strong> Complete enrolment and accept the AI Privacy and Course Usage Agreement to unlock modules, resources, quizzes, and the capstone workspace.</p></div></div><aside class="hero-panel" aria-label="Course snapshot"><div><strong>4–5 hours</strong><span>Total learner effort</span></div><div><strong>8 modules</strong><span>Sequential pathway</span></div><div><strong>55 questions</strong><span>Final randomized quiz</span></div><div><strong>0</strong><span>Prerequisites</span></div></aside></section>
    <section class="section container" id="course-board"><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Course Board</span><h2>At a glance</h2><p>The public course board gives delegates enough information to understand the course before enrolment. Full learning content stays locked until registration and agreement acceptance.</p></div><div class="course-stats"><article class="stat-card"><strong>8</strong><span>Hands-on modules</span></article><article class="stat-card"><strong>5</strong><span>Core use cases</span></article><article class="stat-card"><strong>70%</strong><span>Recommended pass mark</span></article><article class="stat-card"><strong>Capstone</strong><span>Practical evidence</span></article></div></section>
    <section class="section container" id="objectives"><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Learning Objectives</span><h2>What delegates will be able to do</h2></div><div class="objective-list"><div class="objective-row"><b>01</b><span>Explain what Claude is, how it works at a high level, and where its limitations are.</span></div><div class="objective-row"><b>02</b><span>Start and manage conversations across Claude web, desktop, and mobile interfaces.</span></div><div class="objective-row"><b>03</b><span>Apply Claude to writing, summarisation, brainstorming, analysis, and Q&amp;A.</span></div><div class="objective-row"><b>04</b><span>Write clear, specific prompts that consistently produce better results.</span></div><div class="objective-row"><b>05</b><span>Work with approved documents and files and turn outputs into reusable artefacts.</span></div><div class="objective-row"><b>06</b><span>Use Projects, custom instructions, and Memory features responsibly.</span></div><div class="objective-row"><b>07</b><span>Identify when AI output should be verified or used with caution.</span></div><div class="objective-row"><b>08</b><span>Apply at least one Claude workflow to a real task from the learner's role.</span></div></div></section>
    <section class="section container" id="curriculum"><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Public Curriculum</span><h2>Course structure</h2><p>This is the public outline. Full module learning content, interactive activities, resources, assessments, and the capstone workspace unlock after enrolment.</p></div><div class="curriculum-preview"><article class="curriculum-item"><header><h3>01 · Introduction to Claude</h3><strong>25 min</strong></header><p>What Claude is, how it differs from search, and where human judgement remains essential.</p><div class="pill-row"><span class="pill">Capabilities</span><span class="pill">Limitations</span><span class="pill">Responsible use</span></div></article><article class="curriculum-item"><header><h3>02 · Getting Started</h3><strong>30 min</strong></header><p>How to start conversations, give context, and manage useful outputs.</p><div class="pill-row"><span class="pill">Web</span><span class="pill">Desktop</span><span class="pill">Mobile</span></div></article><article class="curriculum-item"><header><h3>03 · Core Use Cases</h3><strong>45 min</strong></header><p>Writing, editing, summarisation, brainstorming, analysis, and Q&amp;A.</p><div class="pill-row"><span class="pill">Writing</span><span class="pill">Summaries</span><span class="pill">Analysis</span></div></article><article class="curriculum-item"><header><h3>04 · Effective Prompting</h3><strong>45 min</strong></header><p>Context, audience, constraints, examples, output format, iteration, and clarifying questions.</p><div class="pill-row"><span class="pill">Prompt framework</span><span class="pill">Examples</span><span class="pill">Iteration</span></div></article><article class="curriculum-item"><header><h3>05 · Documents and Files</h3><strong>40 min</strong></header><p>How to use approved files safely and ask targeted document questions.</p><div class="pill-row"><span class="pill">Documents</span><span class="pill">Artifacts</span><span class="pill">Verification</span></div></article><article class="curriculum-item"><header><h3>06 · Projects and Memory</h3><strong>35 min</strong></header><p>How saved context, custom instructions, and Memory can support recurring work.</p><div class="pill-row"><span class="pill">Projects</span><span class="pill">Instructions</span><span class="pill">Memory</span></div></article><article class="curriculum-item"><header><h3>07 · Best Practices and Pitfalls</h3><strong>35 min</strong></header><p>How to verify outputs, protect information, and avoid over-trusting AI responses.</p><div class="pill-row"><span class="pill">Risk</span><span class="pill">Review</span><span class="pill">Data handling</span></div></article><article class="curriculum-item"><header><h3>08 · Capstone Practice</h3><strong>60 min</strong></header><p>Complete a realistic workplace task using Claude and document the prompt, iteration, output, verification, and application.</p><div class="pill-row"><span class="pill">Practice</span><span class="pill">Capstone</span><span class="pill">Evidence</span></div></article></div></section>
    <section class="section container" id="assessment-info"><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Assessment & Pathway</span><h2>Certification and next step</h2></div><div class="assessment-grid"><article class="resource-card"><h3>Knowledge quiz · 40%</h3><p>A randomized final assessment covering Claude capabilities, limitations, prompting, document workflows, responsible use, and verification.</p></article><article class="resource-card"><h3>Capstone review · 60%</h3><p>A practical workplace task showing the learner's prompt, iteration, output, verification plan, and intended workplace application.</p></article></div><div class="pathway-grid" style="margin-top:16px"><article class="resource-card"><h3>CLD-UF-101 · You are here</h3><p>Foundational, non-technical Claude user course for knowledge workers and business users.</p></article><article class="resource-card"><h3>CLD-DEV-201 · Recommended next</h3><p>Technical follow-on for developers or teams working with the Claude API, tools, and integrations.</p></article></div></section>
    <section class="section container" id="enrol"><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Registration</span><h2>Enrol for CLD-UF-101</h2><p>Submit the registration form below. The enrolment and signed AI Privacy and Course Usage Agreement are emailed to <strong>training@skunkworksacademy.com</strong>.</p></div><form id="enrolmentForm" class="panel form-panel" action="https://formsubmit.co/training@skunkworksacademy.com" method="POST" target="enrolSubmitFrame"><input type="hidden" name="_subject" value="CLD-UF-101 Self-Paced Course Enrolment and AI Usage Agreement" /><input type="hidden" name="_template" value="table" /><input type="hidden" name="_captcha" value="false" /><input type="hidden" name="course" value="CLD-UF-101 Claude User Fundamentals" /><input type="hidden" id="agreementTimestamp" name="agreement_timestamp" value="" /><input type="hidden" id="agreementVersion" name="agreement_version" value="CLD-UF-101 AI Privacy and Course Usage Agreement v1.0" /><input type="hidden" name="agreement_text" value="Delegate accepted the CLD-UF-101 AI Privacy and Course Usage Agreement and confirmed use of enrolment information for administration, learner support, assessment, and certification administration." /><div class="form-grid"><label>First name<input required name="first_name" autocomplete="given-name" /></label><label>Last name<input required name="last_name" autocomplete="family-name" /></label><label>Email<input required type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" /></label><label>Mobile / WhatsApp<input required name="mobile" autocomplete="tel" /></label><label>Company / Organisation<input required name="company" autocomplete="organization" /></label><label>Role / Job title<input required name="role" /></label><label>Country<input required name="country" autocomplete="country-name" /></label><label>Delegate reference / employee number<input required name="delegate_identity_reference" autocomplete="off" /><span class="identity-note">Use an employee number, student number, or another official delegate identifier.</span></label><label>Preferred start date<input type="date" name="preferred_start_date" /></label><label>Manager / sponsor email<input type="email" name="manager_or_sponsor_email" /></label></div><label>Learning goal<textarea name="learning_goal" rows="4" placeholder="Tell us why you want to complete this course."></textarea></label><div class="agreement-scroll"><h3>AI Privacy and Course Usage Agreement</h3><p>I understand that AI tools support learning and productivity, but I remain responsible for verifying outputs, using approved information, and following my organisation's policies.</p><p>I consent to Skunkworks Academy using my enrolment, contact, delegate reference, agreement acknowledgement, course progress, assessment, and capstone information for course administration, support, assessment, and certification administration.</p></div><label class="checkline"><input required id="courseAgreementAccept" type="checkbox" name="agreement_acceptance" value="Accepted" /> I have read, understood, and accept the AI Privacy and Course Usage Agreement.</label><label class="checkline"><input required type="checkbox" name="privacy_acknowledgement" value="Accepted" /> I confirm that my submitted contact and delegate information is accurate.</label><button class="button primary" type="submit">Submit enrolment and unlock course</button><p id="enrolmentStatus" class="form-status" role="status"></p></form><iframe class="hidden-frame" name="enrolSubmitFrame" title="Enrolment submission target"></iframe></section>
    <section class="section container locked-content" id="modules" data-locked-content><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Course Path</span><h2>Interactive modules and knowledge checks</h2><p>Each module includes an activity and a functional mini assessment. Progress is stored in this browser.</p></div><div class="progress-panel panel"><div class="progress-copy"><strong id="progressText">0% complete</strong><span>Mark each module complete after finishing the activity and quiz.</span></div><div class="progress-bar"><div id="progressFill"></div></div></div><div id="moduleGrid" class="module-grid"></div><div id="moduleWorkspace" class="panel workspace" aria-live="polite"></div></section>
    <section class="section container locked-content" id="resources" data-locked-content><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Resources</span><h2>Downloadable course materials</h2></div><div class="resource-grid"><article class="resource-card"><h3>Prompt Library</h3><p>Reusable prompts for writing, summarisation, analysis, document work, Projects, and verification.</p><div class="resource-actions"><button data-export-resource="prompt-library" data-format="pdf">PDF</button><button data-export-resource="prompt-library" data-format="md">MD</button></div></article><article class="resource-card"><h3>Learner Workbook</h3><p>Structured learner workbook for module reflections, prompt practice, and capstone planning.</p><div class="resource-actions"><button data-export-resource="learner-workbook" data-format="pdf">PDF</button><button data-export-resource="learner-workbook" data-format="md">MD</button></div></article><article class="resource-card wide"><h3>Verification Checklist</h3><p>Interactive responsible-use checklist with export options.</p><div id="checklistApp" class="checklist-app"></div><div class="resource-actions wrap"><button data-export-checklist="xlsx">Excel</button><button data-export-checklist="pdf">PDF</button><button data-export-checklist="docx">DOCX</button><button data-export-checklist="pptx">PPTX</button><button data-export-checklist="md">MD</button><button data-export-checklist="html">HTML</button></div></article><article class="resource-card wide" id="agreement"><h3>AI Use Policy User Agreement</h3><p>Your agreement was captured during enrolment and emailed with your delegate registration details.</p><div class="agreement-box"><p id="agreementStatus" class="form-status"></p></div></article></div></section>
    <section class="section container locked-content" id="quiz" data-locked-content><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Final Assessment</span><h2>Final Knowledge Check</h2><p>50 multiple-choice questions are randomized from a 200-question pool. The assessment also includes 5 case-study questions randomized from a 50-question case pool.</p></div><div class="panel quiz-panel"><div class="quiz-actions"><button id="startFinalQuiz" class="button primary" type="button">Start randomized final quiz</button><button id="resetFinalQuiz" class="button secondary" type="button">Reset quiz</button></div><div id="finalQuizApp"></div></div></section>
    <section class="section container locked-content" id="capstone" data-locked-content><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Capstone Project</span><h2>Practical workplace task submission</h2><p>Complete a real or realistic task using Claude. Capture your prompt, iteration, output summary, verification plan, and workplace application.</p></div><div class="panel capstone-panel"><div class="form-grid"><label>Task description<textarea id="capstoneTask" rows="3"></textarea></label><label>Use case selected<textarea id="capstoneUseCase" rows="3"></textarea></label><label>Initial prompt<textarea id="capstonePrompt" rows="4"></textarea></label><label>Follow-up prompt<textarea id="capstoneFollowup" rows="4"></textarea></label><label>Verification list<textarea id="capstoneVerification" rows="4"></textarea></label><label>Workplace application<textarea id="capstoneApplication" rows="4"></textarea></label></div><div class="quiz-actions"><button id="saveCapstone" class="button primary" type="button">Save capstone locally</button><button id="downloadCapstone" class="button secondary" type="button">Download capstone MD</button></div><p id="capstoneStatus" class="form-status"></p></div></section>
